        "description": "Download one remote regular file through the existing SSH SFTP connection with independent remote-read and local-write grants. Supply current scope/resource revisions and epoch, a single remoteName and a relative local destination path. Does not open a new connection or execute a file. Overwrite defaults to false; overwrite=true explicitly permits replacing this target path after rechecks, not conditional replacement of an immutable file identity. Trust other writers of the authorized directory. Replacement uses the temporary file's attributes. Reuse query_transfer/cancel_transfer and retain operationId; retries must keep the same direction and arguments. published/publication and temporary describe the local destination and owned local temporary file. Size and metadata checks do not verify content hashes. Current native local writer is Windows-only; maximum 64 MiB, 64 KiB chunks, 120 seconds overall and 15 seconds without progress between synchronous calls. Remote path checks trust the authorized directory owner and administrator; SFTPv3 cannot prove isolation from same-account malicious path replacement.",
